hi i'm derek downey a developer advocate  for google cloud  i am currently working on developing a  banking application that leverages cloud  spanner the highly scalable managed  relational database from google cloud  in the previous video i set up a  regional spanner instance with a small  amount of compute capacity for  developing my banking application  i also created a customers database on  the instance and all the tables related  to my app will live in this database  now my company might have other internal  only data completely unrelated to my  banking app  that data could be placed in a separate  database because spanner instances can  have multiple databases  databases are a way to organize related  tables together and to provide  additional access control to the data  stored on the instance  for example my banking app should  definitely not have access to the  internal database  besides access control each database can  be configured with different options  that affect the performance recovery and  security of your database  these options control the optimizer  version version retention period and  database encryption  the first database option is the  optimizer version  the optimizer's job is to create an  execution plan that is an efficient way  to retrieve data from spanner based on  the given sql query  it has a direct impact on performance of  requests issued to your database  over time the query optimizer will  change to improve the accuracy of the  estimates required to create this  execution plan  when spanner releases a new optimizer  version the default behavior is for  databases to use the new version 30 days  after release  optimizer versions can change the  performance of your query workload  so it's important to compare query  performance of the new version with the  older version  you can pin the optimizer version a  database uses to a specific version by  altering the database  altering the database optimizer version  to null resets to the default behavior  of updating 30 days after the release of  a new version  you can also change the optimizer  version for individual queries by  providing the optimizer version query  hint  this is useful to validate queries where  stable performance is critical without  changing the optimizer version for the  entire database  another important database option is the  version retention period which affects  the ability to perform a point in time  recovery  by default spanner will maintain all  versions of the data and schema for one  hour in my banking application i want to  protect against accidental data loss  with spanner's default retention i have  an hour to copy the data as it existed  before an accidental change and then  load it back into the database  during normal business operations this  hour might be enough  but what about during off hours or the  weekend  i might not be able to respond in time  to avoid data loss  so i want to be sure to size my version  retention period to give my team enough  time to recover outside of normal hours  one way to do this would be to set the  version retention period according to my  backup frequency  for instance if i take a backup of my  database once a day then i will want to  set my version retention period to one  day  the last option i will cover is how  encryption is handled for spanner  databases  all data in spanner is encrypted at rest  by default this encryption is handled  for you by google cloud  however if you have specific compliance  or regulatory requirements on the keys  encrypting the data spanner offers the  ability to deploy your own encryption  keys  these are called customer managed  encryption keys and are managed through  google cloud kms  it is possible to have some databases  configured with customer encryption keys  while other databases on the same  instance use google cloud to manage  encryption  up and managing these custom encryption  keys is beyond the scope of this video  but there are some important pieces of  information when using custom encryption  keys  first a database must be created with  the custom encryption key  custom encryption keys cannot be enabled  on an existing database  second for backups the primary version  of the encryption key at the time of  backup creation  is used to encrypt backups  finally encryption keys must be  available to decrypt the database and  backups  if a key is deleted and can't be  recovered any spanner database or backup  encrypted with that key is unrecoverable  for now i will be using the default  encryption managed by google cloud for  my banking application  cloud spanner offers the ability to  organize related data into multiple  databases on your spanner instance  this provides some additional control  over who has access to the data stored  there  in this video i went over some other  options that give you more control over  the performance recovery and security of  your spanner database in our next video  i will go into more detail about the  spanner schema including data types data  organization and schema management  in the meantime please let us know in  the comments if you have any questions  around database specific options in  spanner  [Music]  you
 

